// HVM4 expands a recursive definition's reference eagerly, without waiting for
// its match to be able to fire.  So it normalises closed terms and diverges on
// any open term whose free variable a recursive function scrutinises.
//
// This is the whole reason normalising a recursive TYPE FAMILY under a binder
// diverges: the family's body reaches `compose`, which reaches `permAt`, which
// reaches `nth`, on the bound element.  Nothing about the diameter statement is
// at fault, and the Bend checker reduces Diameter(twenty()) in full.
//
// Measured with hvm4 @ 6defdfc:
//
//   @main = @loop(#Con{1,#Con{2,#Nil}})   ->  0, in 12 interactions
//   @main = #Sig{#Unit, Lq. @loop(q)}     ->  does not terminate
//   @main = #Sig{#Unit, Lq. @peel(q)}     ->  1 interaction, stays stuck, prints
//
// @loop and @peel differ only in the recursive call.

@loop = λxs. (λ{#Nil: 0; #Con: λh. λt. @loop(t)})(xs)
@peel = λxs. (λ{#Nil: 0; #Con: λh. λt. h})(xs)

@main = #Sig{#Unit, λq. @peel(q)}
